00:24:12,361 --> 00:24:13,763
She's a monster.

518
00:24:13,897 --> 00:24:15,398
However, in order to get

519
00:24:15,531 --> 00:24:17,200
the unpalatable deal
that I want,

520
00:24:17,333 --> 00:24:19,002
I will need to look Salazar
in the eye.

521
00:24:19,135 --> 00:24:20,003
Hello?

522
00:24:20,469 --> 00:24:21,437
Hello?

523
00:24:21,571 --> 00:24:22,538
Oh, Mr. Horowitz,

524
00:24:22,706 --> 00:24:24,539
how lovely to hear from you.

525
00:24:24,540 --> 00:24:25,508
Okay, sweetheart.

526
00:24:26,876 --> 00:24:28,778
200. That's it.

527
00:24:28,912 --> 00:24:31,247
Has anyone ever told you
you have a wonderful timbre

528
00:24:31,380 --> 00:24:32,481
to your voice.

529
00:24:33,082 --> 00:24:34,517
I'm trying to place it.

530
00:24:34,651 --> 00:24:35,518
That's funny?

531
00:24:35,719 --> 00:24:36,753
200 is funny.

532
00:24:36,886 --> 00:24:38,521
I got it.

533
00:24:38,722 --> 00:24:41,290
From the 1950s hit
The African Queen

534
00:24:41,424 --> 00:24:43,927
starring Katherine Hepburn
and Humphrey Bogart.

535
00:24:44,093 --> 00:24:46,062
You sound just like
Katherine Hepburn.

536
00:24:46,696 --> 00:24:47,563
Okay.

537
00:24:49,899 --> 00:24:50,934
300.

538
00:24:51,167 --> 00:24:52,702
I wanna sit down with Salazar.

539
00:24:52,836 --> 00:24:55,171
Since I can't talk to you,
I wanna talk to him.

540
00:24:55,438 --> 00:24:58,307
What?! You f... You fu...

541
00:24:58,441 --> 00:25:00,710
You fucking cu...

542
00:25:00,844 --> 00:25:02,311
Salam Alaikum.

543
00:25:02,445 --> 00:25:03,780
Salazar doesn't know it yet,

544
00:25:03,913 --> 00:25:05,581
but he's going to agree
to a meeting.

545
00:25:05,715 --> 00:25:07,216
It's gonna happen on the island.

546
00:25:07,450 --> 00:25:09,385
That's the only place
he'll feel safe.

547
00:25:09,518 --> 00:25:12,455
It's just a question of when,
but there's still plenty of time

548
00:25:12,622 --> 00:25:14,257
for you and your boys to put
in the infrastructure

549
00:25:14,390 --> 00:25:15,591
and prepare for the worst.

550
00:25:15,725 --> 00:25:16,793
Bronco?

551
00:25:17,426 --> 00:25:18,795
I'm sure you've had
a sniff around.

552
00:25:19,195 --> 00:25:20,229
How do we feel about that?

553
00:25:20,396 --> 00:25:21,631
I think we feel okay.

554
00:25:22,031 --> 00:25:23,099
Okay.

555
00:25:23,232 --> 00:25:24,100
Better get more boots then.

556
00:25:30,206 --> 00:25:31,174
Phase two.

557
00:25:31,374 --> 00:25:32,842
Planning and preparation.

558
00:25:39,916 --> 00:25:41,217
Mr. Beauregard.

559
00:25:42,151 --> 00:25:43,687
Buenos días, Captain Sensible.

560
00:25:43,887 --> 00:25:44,854
Love the shirt.

561
00:25:45,121 --> 00:25:45,889
It's silk.

562
00:25:46,790 --> 00:25:47,590
Like my sheets.

563
00:25:48,725 --> 00:25:49,693
Course it is.

564
00:25:49,959 --> 00:25:51,427
My insurance policy

565
00:25:51,560 --> 00:25:52,195
will need to consist
of a full team.

566
00:25:52,328 --> 00:25:53,963
Baker...

567
00:25:54,397 --> 00:25:55,398
Baker will be in charge
of explosives

568
00:25:55,564 --> 00:25:56,766
and munitions.

569
00:25:57,500 --> 00:26:00,536
Moreno is a wheel man in charge
of on-ground transport.

570
00:26:00,904 --> 00:26:04,173
Dunne is in charge of
aviation... and cynicism.

571
00:26:04,407 --> 00:26:05,641
This is Gucci.

572
00:26:05,775 --> 00:26:06,609
He's in charge of tech.

573
00:26:09,813 --> 00:26:11,014
I just told you.

574
00:26:11,147 --> 00:26:12,849
It's silk.

575
00:26:12,982 --> 00:26:14,250
Their principal agenda

576
00:26:14,517 --> 00:26:16,019
will be getting me
off the island

577
00:26:16,152 --> 00:26:17,420
and should I need
to leave quickly,

578
00:26:17,586 --> 00:26:19,689
they'll need a full chest
of toys.

579
00:26:19,823 --> 00:26:21,925
Indigenous ambulance,
40,000 on the clock,

580
00:26:22,091 --> 00:26:25,461
full tank of laughing gas
and four brand new boots.

581
00:26:25,829 --> 00:26:27,530
Baker, door.

582
00:26:30,033 --> 00:26:31,434
Abracadabra.

583
00:26:31,567 --> 00:26:33,302
Say hello to Javier.

584
00:26:33,436 --> 00:26:35,905
- Hello, Javier.
- Hola, chicos.

585
00:26:36,039 --> 00:26:38,808
He's been a very clever boy
and got the full shopping list.

586
00:26:39,008 --> 00:26:43,012
Two canoes, four oars,
two emergency outboards.

587
00:26:43,146 --> 00:26:47,516
Late 2010 coche,
upgraded with an LS3 V8.

588
00:26:47,817 --> 00:26:50,086
Three KTM 450s.

589
00:26:50,219 --> 00:26:53,456
125 scooter for eggs
and fresh milk.

590
00:26:53,656 --> 00:26:57,994
Two Polaris Razors with 190hp
and plenty of torque.

591
00:26:59,062 --> 00:27:00,396
And Teddy for fishing.

592
00:27:00,663 --> 00:27:03,032
We've got a full set
of knives and forks.

593
00:27:03,166 --> 00:27:04,100
We've got your reach out
and touch me

594
00:27:04,233 --> 00:27:05,501
for the long range slot.

595
00:27:05,735 --> 00:27:08,337
Noise makers, cloudies, blinders.

596
00:27:08,471 --> 00:27:11,841
We've got 9-mils and 45s
avec hush puppies.

597
00:27:12,208 --> 00:27:14,744
Gucci AR with a 203
grenade launcher.

598
00:27:15,044 --> 00:27:17,747
Brand new boom stick
with 40-mil butt plugs.

599
00:27:17,881 --> 00:27:18,982
Top cigars
for the Charlie Gs

600
00:27:19,148 --> 00:27:20,249
for ground to air.

601
00:27:20,383 --> 00:27:21,684
And finally...

602
00:27:22,218 --> 00:27:25,288
24 ice cold
cervezas.

603
00:27:25,588 --> 00:27:26,890
Please drink responsibly.

604
00:27:27,590 --> 00:27:28,724
Alright ladies,
don't get excited

605
00:27:28,858 --> 00:27:29,793
about our accommodation.

606
00:27:29,926 --> 00:27:31,127
It's not the Savoy.

607
00:27:31,527 --> 00:27:32,862
We're hidden in
the most remote part

608
00:27:33,029 --> 00:27:34,430
of Salazar's Island.

609
00:27:34,864 --> 00:27:36,866
We chose this safe house
due to its proximity

610
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:40,636
to all three extraction points
and its historical tunnels,

611
00:27:40,770 --> 00:27:42,705
should we need to get
Rachel out discreetly.

612
00:27:42,839 --> 00:27:46,175
Rachel is only ever going to be
in one of two places.

613
00:27:46,442 --> 00:27:47,743
Either here at the villa,

614
00:27:48,011 --> 00:27:49,378
or at Salazar's hotel.

615
00:27:49,745 --> 00:27:51,881
He lives in the penthouse suite

616
00:27:52,048 --> 00:27:53,482
which is where they will meet.

617
00:27:53,716 --> 00:27:55,751
If things get exciting,

618
00:27:55,885 --> 00:27:56,820
we extract Mum,

619
00:27:56,953 --> 00:27:58,121
assess the threat level,

620
00:27:58,287 --> 00:27:59,555
bring her back to the villa

621
00:27:59,789 --> 00:28:00,990
and get her off the island.

622
00:28:01,124 --> 00:28:02,792
Three extraction points.

623
00:28:03,192 --> 00:28:04,593
If we need to move
Rachel from the hotel,

624
00:28:04,727 --> 00:28:06,629
we take the east evac route.

625
00:28:06,863 --> 00:28:09,165
We'll take the SUVs through the
town through the storm drains

626
00:28:09,298 --> 00:28:10,766
to two awaiting RIBs.

627
00:28:11,034 --> 00:28:12,836
If we need to extract her
from the villa,

628
00:28:12,969 --> 00:28:14,770
we go from an airfield
on the north of the island.

629
00:28:14,904 --> 00:28:16,239
Jets and helicopters
are a no-go

630
00:28:16,372 --> 00:28:18,407
because Salazar controls
the skies.

631
00:28:18,574 --> 00:28:20,276
That's why we came here
by boat.

632
00:28:20,409 --> 00:28:22,078
We have
two gyrocopters waiting.

633
00:28:22,211 --> 00:28:23,346
They'll go undetected.

634
00:28:23,813 --> 00:28:25,681
The west evac
is our last resort.

635
00:28:25,815 --> 00:28:28,251
There's no other way
off the island.

636
00:28:28,384 --> 00:28:31,187
Each route has its own
challenges but we need to reach

637
00:28:31,320 --> 00:28:33,923
these points as quickly
and efficiently as possible.

638
00:28:34,457 --> 00:28:36,125
We're gonna be ready
for any eventuality

639
00:28:36,259 --> 00:28:37,560
and practice until
we get it right.

640
00:28:37,726 --> 00:28:41,430
But this is Salazar's Island.

641
00:28:41,564 --> 00:28:43,299
The police are on payroll

642
00:28:43,632 --> 00:28:46,735
and he has a reasonably
experienced private army.

643
00:28:46,970 --> 00:28:48,905
- How many?
- Best guess, 50.

644
00:28:49,438 --> 00:28:51,941
- What's that all about?
- Considering his activities,

645
00:28:52,141 --> 00:28:54,510
he takes some comfort
from having a small militia.

646
00:28:54,643 --> 00:28:56,145
The police station
is an issue.

647
00:28:56,279 --> 00:28:57,780
If anyone ends up inside,
we need to know

648
00:28:57,914 --> 00:28:58,781
how to get 'em out.

649
00:28:58,915 --> 00:28:59,949
Where do you wanna start?

650
00:29:00,116 --> 00:29:01,817
Well, first we recce the routes

651
00:29:01,951 --> 00:29:03,686
and then we go look at the hotel
and the police station.

652
00:29:03,819 --> 00:29:04,820
We'll split up.

653
00:29:04,954 --> 00:29:06,089
Gucci, Dunne and Baker,

654
00:29:06,255 --> 00:29:07,857
you recce the north evac point

655
00:29:07,991 --> 00:29:09,625
and log a flight time
to the mainland.

656
00:29:09,758 --> 00:29:13,229
Bronco, Moreno and yours truly.

657
00:29:13,796 --> 00:29:16,232
We'll recce the fastest route
from Salazar's penthouse

658
00:29:16,832 --> 00:29:19,601
through the city
to the east evac point.

659
00:29:22,671 --> 00:29:24,740
Hey, Captain Sensible,
can you, er,

660
00:29:24,874 --> 00:29:26,209
can you just slow down
a little bit?

661
00:29:26,342 --> 00:29:27,310
You're starting
to make me nervous.

662
00:29:29,645 --> 00:29:31,114
Time really does stand still...

663
00:29:32,148 --> 00:29:33,316
when I'm with you.

664
00:29:33,449 --> 00:29:34,483
Dunno what you're
so grumpy about.

665
00:29:34,617 --> 00:29:35,818
You planned the route.

666
00:29:38,888 --> 00:29:41,891
If we're not careful,
your dad's gonna blow our cover.

667
00:29:44,460 --> 00:29:47,029
- Okay. Thank you.
- Okay.

668
00:29:47,030 --> 00:29:48,664
Tell your dad not
to spend it all at once.

669
00:29:53,136 --> 00:29:54,737
Are you thinking
what I'm thinking?

670
00:29:55,171 --> 00:29:57,706
That two wheels
is better than four.

671
00:29:58,507 --> 00:30:00,076
Okay, sweethearts,
we'll run the full route

672
00:30:00,209 --> 00:30:01,510
to the east evacuation point.

673
00:30:01,644 --> 00:30:02,511
If we need to get her out,

674
00:30:02,645 --> 00:30:03,746
Mom will be transported

675
00:30:03,913 --> 00:30:05,114
on the back of the bike.

676
00:30:11,087 --> 00:30:12,721
We've got a police car
up ahead.

677
00:30:12,855 --> 00:30:13,856
Who wants to kick 'em
in the ass

678
00:30:13,990 --> 00:30:14,857
and see if they'll kick back?

679
00:30:14,991 --> 00:30:15,891
Leave it with me.

680
00:30:16,025 --> 00:30:17,026
Good man, Moreno.

681
00:30:17,160 --> 00:30:18,294
Try not to end up in jail.

682
00:30:26,269 --> 00:30:27,570
Head to
the storm drains.

683
00:30:27,836 --> 00:30:29,272
See if they have
the stomach to follow.

684
00:30:32,741 --> 00:30:33,776
This is
too fuckin' easy.

685
00:30:34,944 --> 00:30:36,479
What I need is a pig on a bike.

686
00:30:44,620 --> 00:30:46,389
Moreno, what the fuck
are you doing?

687
00:30:46,522 --> 00:30:47,957
You do your thing,
let me do mine.

688
00:30:49,758 --> 00:30:50,994
Looks like your
dream's come true.

689
00:30:51,294 --> 00:30:52,761
You've picked up a pig
on two wheels.

690
00:30:52,962 --> 00:30:54,964
Yep, thank you!

691
00:31:01,537 --> 00:31:04,140
You know, surprisingly he's not
completely shit, this guy.

692
00:31:08,111 --> 00:31:09,478
Let's see if this fucker
likes the idea

693
00:31:09,712 --> 00:31:11,080
of dropping twenty foot
into a storm drain.

694
00:31:24,193 --> 00:31:25,594
Sadly, he didn't follow.

695
00:31:25,728 --> 00:31:26,729
Coming in beside you.

696
00:31:32,968 --> 00:31:34,337
Turns out
you do actually

697
00:31:34,470 --> 00:31:35,704
have some talents, Moreno.

698
00:31:43,746 --> 00:31:45,781
Okay. Looks like
that'll work if we need it to.

699
00:31:45,914 --> 00:31:47,350
So, a boat will
pick us up from here?

700
00:31:47,516 --> 00:31:48,651
That's the idea.

701
00:31:49,018 --> 00:31:50,353
But the bikes won't work
if we need

702
00:31:50,486 --> 00:31:51,954
to take someone
who's incapacitated.

703
00:31:52,188 --> 00:31:54,723
For that, we'll need
the ambulance to get us

704
00:31:54,857 --> 00:31:56,392
through town and an ATV
to get us down the storm drain.

705
00:31:56,625 --> 00:31:58,194
Then we get them off on a RIB.

706
00:31:59,162 --> 00:32:00,863
Okay,
so onto the next route.

707
00:32:00,996 --> 00:32:02,565
North evac is a straight shot

708
00:32:02,698 --> 00:32:04,500
through a wind farm
outside the city.

709
00:32:04,633 --> 00:32:07,636
It is our primary extraction
point as our gyrocopters

710
00:32:07,770 --> 00:32:10,139
are the fastest way
to get Rachel off the island.

711
00:32:10,273 --> 00:32:12,508
We'll need to get these
operational and onto the runway

712
00:32:12,641 --> 00:32:14,277
in no more than three minutes.

713
00:32:14,677 --> 00:32:17,480
The only way to do that
is to rehearse.

714
00:32:29,892 --> 00:32:32,994
It takes 25 minutes
to get to the mainland.

715
00:32:32,995 --> 00:32:34,463
Twenty five minutes?

716
00:32:34,830 --> 00:32:36,432
Give me something faster,
I'll get it there quicker.

717
00:32:36,565 --> 00:32:37,800
How long from the hotel?

718
00:32:38,167 --> 00:32:39,268
Got it down to nine
and a half minutes.

719
00:32:39,402 --> 00:32:40,703
Get it down to eight and a half.

720
00:32:40,836 --> 00:32:42,238
That's not possible.

721
00:32:42,471 --> 00:32:43,939
You're right, six and a half
is possible.

722
00:32:44,073 --> 00:32:45,241
This is how we're
gonna do it.

723
00:32:45,374 --> 00:32:46,275
We'll take Rachel
from the hotel.

724
00:32:46,409 --> 00:32:47,510
These have to be out of the shed

725
00:32:47,643 --> 00:32:49,112
and in the air in three minutes.

726
00:32:49,245 --> 00:32:51,880
You two pilot and take Rachel
and me with you.

727
00:32:52,014 --> 00:32:55,017
If this doesn't work,
we go to the west evac.

728
00:32:55,651 --> 00:32:57,353
That means back to the villa,

729
00:32:57,486 --> 00:32:58,554
through the tunnel,

730
00:32:59,255 --> 00:33:01,690
onto the bikes
until it's easier by foot.

731
00:33:01,824 --> 00:33:03,792
Then there's an obstacle.

732
00:33:03,926 --> 00:33:07,430
The upside of the obstacle
is no-one can follow us.

733
00:33:07,596 --> 00:33:10,399
But the downside of
the obstacle is, er...

734
00:33:12,501 --> 00:33:13,269
That's the straightest line?

735
00:33:14,770 --> 00:33:15,704
Fuck off.

736
00:33:16,939 --> 00:33:18,507
I foresee a problem.

737
00:33:18,774 --> 00:33:20,543
Point A, the villa is two
and a half miles that way.

738
00:33:20,676 --> 00:33:21,877
Point B, the west evac point

739
00:33:22,044 --> 00:33:23,712
is seven and a half miles
that way.

740
00:33:23,846 --> 00:33:25,047
This is the straightest line.

741
00:33:28,016 --> 00:33:30,153
Now, I am aware that
there is a 300-foot deep

742
00:33:30,286 --> 00:33:31,954
untraversable ravine before you.

743
00:33:33,289 --> 00:33:35,224
But fortunately,

744
00:33:35,358 --> 00:33:37,726
Baker and I have put a great
deal of thought into this.

745
00:33:37,893 --> 00:33:41,197
And we've discovered that if you
give yourself enough runway,

746
00:33:41,864 --> 00:33:43,366
build up some speed,

747
00:33:43,699 --> 00:33:45,201
and flap your arms like so...

748
00:33:50,038 --> 00:33:52,208
It should take the bump
out of the landing.

749
00:33:54,310 --> 00:33:57,446
Alternatively, there is another
option for the less adventurous.

750
00:34:01,384 --> 00:34:03,286
It's, er, called a zipline.

751
00:34:07,590 --> 00:34:09,858
The zipline takes us
to where our ATVs are hidden.

752
00:34:12,295 --> 00:34:12,928
Then there's the matter
of getting to the harbour

753
00:34:13,095 --> 00:34:14,763
as quickly as possible.

754
00:34:15,164 --> 00:34:16,932
And like with
the other routes,

755
00:34:17,300 --> 00:34:18,467
we'll need to time
and rehearse this too.

756
00:34:21,136 --> 00:34:22,070
Do it again!

757
00:34:37,986 --> 00:34:40,022
- What happened there?
- I can do better.

758
00:34:40,155 --> 00:34:41,856
Go on. Fuck off.

759
00:34:41,857 --> 00:34:43,692
Jesus! Fuck!

760
00:34:44,527 --> 00:34:45,294
Door.

761
00:34:47,430 --> 00:34:48,331
Four minutes.

762
00:34:51,767 --> 00:34:52,935
Four feet to the left.

763
00:34:55,404 --> 00:34:56,405
Three feet to the left.

764
00:34:58,207 --> 00:34:59,542
Two feet to the left.

765
00:35:07,450 --> 00:35:08,217
Bingo.

766
00:35:17,192 --> 00:35:18,060
Do it again.

767
00:35:20,963 --> 00:35:21,964
Four minutes.

768
00:35:22,197 --> 00:35:23,198
Not too shabby.

769
00:35:23,366 --> 00:35:24,433
Let's go again.

770
00:35:27,303 --> 00:35:28,571
Argh, dammit!

771
00:35:32,207 --> 00:35:33,842
2:59. Got it.

772
00:35:33,976 --> 00:35:35,511
Aaargh!

773
00:35:37,913 --> 00:35:39,982
Three, two, one...

774
00:35:45,354 --> 00:35:46,422
Not bad.

775
00:35:53,862 --> 00:35:55,731
In contingency, if the north
evac fails

776
00:35:55,864 --> 00:35:56,899
and we have pursuing vehicles,

777
00:35:57,032 --> 00:35:59,435
we lead them into a banana pie.

778
00:35:59,568 --> 00:36:02,070
There'll be one vehicle
