1283
01:03:49,403 --> 01:03:50,171
Shereen!

1284
01:04:17,531 --> 01:04:18,565
Hello, my lovely.

1285
01:05:07,748 --> 01:05:08,815
Who the fuck are you?

1286
01:05:12,486 --> 01:05:13,687
You can't just walk
into my office!

1287
01:05:14,621 --> 01:05:15,789
Oh yes, we can.

1288
01:05:15,922 --> 01:05:18,025
I've got security cameras.

1289
01:05:18,159 --> 01:05:18,992
There are people watching.

1290
01:05:19,926 --> 01:05:20,827
No, there aren't.

1291
01:05:22,863 --> 01:05:23,797
So, who are you?

1292
01:05:26,100 --> 01:05:26,800
What do you want?

1293
01:05:28,602 --> 01:05:29,770
Salazar's taken Rachel.

1294
01:05:31,372 --> 01:05:34,308
Oh... all right.

1295
01:05:35,642 --> 01:05:37,978
You're her boys, I see.
Well, that's kind of sweet.

1296
01:05:40,214 --> 01:05:41,382
It's being handled.

1297
01:05:41,848 --> 01:05:42,883
Everything's being handled.

1298
01:05:44,185 --> 01:05:46,453
How... exactly?

1299
01:05:48,655 --> 01:05:49,856
We're dealing with the Ministry
of Foreign Affairs,

1300
01:05:49,990 --> 01:05:51,192
we're talking to
the State Department,

1301
01:05:51,458 --> 01:05:53,160
we're dealing with
the Spanish police.

1302
01:05:53,327 --> 01:05:55,996
It's a... it's a highly complex
and evolving situation.

1303
01:05:56,130 --> 01:05:58,031
So, you're doing nothing.

1304
01:05:58,165 --> 01:06:01,168
Look, we all just
have to be patient

1305
01:06:01,302 --> 01:06:03,036
and Salazar will
get his toys back.

1306
01:06:03,170 --> 01:06:05,005
Rachel gets released.
She gets paid...

1307
01:06:05,139 --> 01:06:06,340
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

1308
01:06:10,077 --> 01:06:12,379
So, you're telling me that
she got you your money back

1309
01:06:12,513 --> 01:06:13,914
and she still
hasn't been paid?

1310
01:06:14,315 --> 01:06:15,482
That's not very nice.

1311
01:06:15,649 --> 01:06:18,319
Look, you stick to the dancing

1312
01:06:19,253 --> 01:06:20,421
and I'll do the thinking.

1313
01:06:20,654 --> 01:06:21,988
Don't be cute.

1314
01:06:22,856 --> 01:06:24,358
Nothing is as simple
as it seems.

1315
01:06:25,259 --> 01:06:26,260
Yes, it is.

1316
01:06:28,395 --> 01:06:29,196
Pay your debts.

1317
01:06:57,924 --> 01:07:01,895
Miss Wild, we made an agreement.

1318
01:07:02,729 --> 01:07:04,797
I kept my side.

1319
01:07:04,798 --> 01:07:06,733
Spencer Goldstein have not.

1320
01:07:06,867 --> 01:07:08,702
No, it's not that simple.

1321
01:07:09,303 --> 01:07:11,238
They have something
really valuable to me.

1322
01:07:11,638 --> 01:07:13,474
Now I have something
valuable to them.

1323
01:07:15,209 --> 01:07:17,778
No, you... you don't.

1324
01:07:18,479 --> 01:07:20,781
Even if they knew that I'm here,
well, they wouldn't care.

1325
01:07:20,947 --> 01:07:22,349
It won't register.

1326
01:07:22,616 --> 01:07:24,818
I'm worth less to them
than a stray dog.

1327
01:07:25,919 --> 01:07:27,988
Quite brilliantly,
you're worth billions.

1328
01:07:29,122 --> 01:07:30,824
But they manage trillions.

1329
01:07:30,957 --> 01:07:32,959
If they owned New York City,
you'd just be a...

1330
01:07:34,628 --> 01:07:36,096
a hot dog stand.

1331
01:07:36,630 --> 01:07:39,999
Holding me gets you nowhere.

1332
01:07:40,000 --> 01:07:41,602
And they're never going
to pay you.

1333
01:07:42,669 --> 01:07:44,238
They haven't even paid me.

1334
01:07:47,241 --> 01:07:48,242
We'll see.

1335
01:07:52,313 --> 01:07:53,614
You will find a way
to make them.

1336
01:07:55,616 --> 01:07:59,386
Otherwise parts of you
are going to start turning up

1337
01:07:59,520 --> 01:08:01,222
in their New York office.

1338
01:08:01,755 --> 01:08:03,390
This is my island, Rachel.

1339
01:08:03,524 --> 01:08:06,092
My police, my law.

1340
01:08:06,793 --> 01:08:08,161
I have an entire army
to make sure

1341
01:08:08,295 --> 01:08:09,596
no-one's coming to save you.

1342
01:08:26,780 --> 01:08:28,582
The tracker's saying she's
still at the police station?

1343
01:08:28,715 --> 01:08:30,384
She's there.
It's confirmed.

1344
01:08:31,718 --> 01:08:33,186
Are we still set
for Plan A?

1345
01:08:33,554 --> 01:08:35,522
Yes, everything
is still in place.

1346
01:08:35,822 --> 01:08:38,392
I've put the engine killers
back on the police cars.

1347
01:08:38,692 --> 01:08:40,427
I've got the zipline working.

1348
01:08:40,661 --> 01:08:42,663
The spikes are back
in their original place.

1349
01:08:43,196 --> 01:08:45,666
So are the landmines.
Even the trap.

1350
01:08:47,801 --> 01:08:49,069
Have the numbers changed?

1351
01:08:49,336 --> 01:08:51,071
Salazar
has increased security,

1352
01:08:51,238 --> 01:08:53,774
so be prepared to improvise.

1353
01:08:53,907 --> 01:08:56,109
There's an extra unit
at the hotel.

1354
01:08:56,243 --> 01:09:00,614
One mobile patrol and
around 20 men at the station.

1355
01:09:00,747 --> 01:09:04,150
Now they change shift, so
there's a perfect time to go.

1356
01:09:04,885 --> 01:09:06,853
But I warn you,
these guys are professional

1357
01:09:06,987 --> 01:09:07,988
and they're ready for trouble.

1358
01:09:10,457 --> 01:09:12,726
Hey. Do you wanna change first?

1359
01:09:19,566 --> 01:09:21,568
We'll lead in the police car.

1360
01:09:21,768 --> 01:09:24,771
Moreno, Baker, you take
the back roads in the Jeep.

1361
01:09:25,372 --> 01:09:27,608
Gucci and Dunne, you take
the RIB to the airfield.

1362
01:09:27,774 --> 01:09:29,142
Everybody clear
how we're doing this?

1363
01:09:29,276 --> 01:09:30,711
- Yes, Sir.
- Stealth.

1364
01:09:30,844 --> 01:09:33,079
Armory. Rachel.
Exit the way we came in.

1365
01:09:33,213 --> 01:09:34,815
And Moreno, you've got up front.

1366
01:09:34,948 --> 01:09:37,050
- Keep eyes out for any movement.
- Copy.

1367
01:09:37,183 --> 01:09:39,019
We'll rendezvous with Dunne
and Gucci at the airfield.

1368
01:09:39,252 --> 01:09:41,888
Dunne, you'll have Rachel in the
air eight minutes from pick-up.

1369
01:09:42,055 --> 01:09:43,390
- Got it.
- Gucci, you've got Sid.

1370
01:09:43,557 --> 01:09:45,559
Then everybody else with me
providing cover.

1371
01:09:45,692 --> 01:09:47,861
And when they are airborne,
we fall back to the west evac.

1372
01:09:48,094 --> 01:09:48,862
Copy that.

1373
01:09:51,365 --> 01:09:52,799
Approaching the rear
of the police station.

1374
01:09:55,769 --> 01:09:57,237
Dropping off Baker to stand by.

1375
01:10:00,273 --> 01:10:02,876
- Bronco, Sid, what's your ETA?
- Thirty seconds out.

1376
01:10:03,243 --> 01:10:03,944
Copy.

1377
01:10:06,079 --> 01:10:07,314
That's Baker on foot.

1378
01:10:10,283 --> 01:10:11,652
Twenty seconds out.

1379
01:10:13,053 --> 01:10:14,921
Moving into position for
surveillance of the front door.

1380
01:10:18,325 --> 01:10:19,826
Ten seconds out.

1381
01:10:20,093 --> 01:10:22,195
Still quiet out front, boys.

1382
01:10:22,329 --> 01:10:25,898
Couple of tangos idling.
Shouldn't be a problem.

1383
01:10:25,899 --> 01:10:27,834
- We're pulling up.
- Copy. Eyes on.

1384
01:10:54,995 --> 01:10:55,762
Ch-ch!

1385
01:10:58,599 --> 01:11:00,000
Manos arriba!

1386
01:11:06,039 --> 01:11:07,974
All quiet,
no movement out front.

1387
01:11:20,286 --> 01:11:21,187
Oh...

1388
01:11:24,391 --> 01:11:25,526
Manos... arriba.

1389
01:11:27,461 --> 01:11:29,962
Manos arriba. Arriba.

1390
01:11:29,963 --> 01:11:31,865
Don't fuckin' think about it.

1391
01:11:31,998 --> 01:11:33,266
Uh!

1392
01:11:39,573 --> 01:11:41,174
We've got incoming, boys.

1393
01:11:41,307 --> 01:11:42,676
One car approaching
the compound.

1394
01:11:46,012 --> 01:11:47,047
Pulling up now.

1395
01:11:50,917 --> 01:11:52,285
He's sitting in the car.

1396
01:11:53,019 --> 01:11:54,387
I'll let you know
when he exits.

1397
01:12:02,696 --> 01:12:03,897
Still no movement.

1398
01:12:06,700 --> 01:12:08,368
Stand against the wall
and stay there.

1399
01:12:15,375 --> 01:12:17,176
Still good on the front door.

1400
01:12:25,218 --> 01:12:27,187
Ah, ah, ah, ah, ah, ah!

1401
01:12:27,420 --> 01:12:29,089
- Ugh!
- Manos arriba.

1402
01:12:29,923 --> 01:12:31,424
Up! You too.

1403
01:12:33,627 --> 01:12:35,028
Three officers coming
in the side door.

1404
01:12:36,463 --> 01:12:37,297
Ten seconds out.

1405
01:12:41,568 --> 01:12:42,235
Five seconds out.

1406
01:12:53,747 --> 01:12:55,716
You've got two more coming
through the front door.

1407
01:12:55,982 --> 01:12:58,251
- Bronco, more incoming.
- It's on you.

1408
01:13:00,053 --> 01:13:01,221
Manos arriba.

1409
01:13:03,590 --> 01:13:04,891
¡Manos arriba!

1410
01:13:11,998 --> 01:13:12,799
Uh, uh, uh...

1411
01:13:17,337 --> 01:13:18,839
Don't fuckin' do it.

1412
01:13:20,273 --> 01:13:21,608
Fuck it!

1413
01:13:24,745 --> 01:13:26,847
You got incoming, boys.
It's starting to get busy.

1414
01:13:26,980 --> 01:13:28,148
We can't get out the front!

1415
01:13:28,281 --> 01:13:30,050
Baker, stand by for plan B.

1416
01:13:41,795 --> 01:13:42,863
Blow the back door!

1417
01:13:44,798 --> 01:13:46,499
Oh, my God.

1418
01:13:46,633 --> 01:13:48,268
- Come on.
- Okay.

1419
01:13:49,870 --> 01:13:51,237
Move, move, move!

1420
01:13:57,210 --> 01:13:58,378
Moreno, get the fucking
car around!

1421
01:13:58,545 --> 01:13:59,713
Movin'!

1422
01:14:08,955 --> 01:14:10,056
Okay. Let's go.

1423
01:14:12,025 --> 01:14:13,660
Dunne,
we are en route to the airfield.

1424
01:14:13,794 --> 01:14:14,761
Get the gyros ready.

1425
01:14:25,639 --> 01:14:26,539
They got the girl.

1426
01:14:28,208 --> 01:14:29,409
What do you mean,
"They got the girl"?

1427
01:14:29,576 --> 01:14:30,844
They broke her out of prison

1428
01:14:31,144 --> 01:14:32,212
and they're trying
to leave the island.

1429
01:14:32,378 --> 01:14:33,379
Well, stop them!

1430
01:14:38,318 --> 01:14:39,720
And get her back!

1431
01:14:42,756 --> 01:14:44,357
If we wanna strand them,
now's our chance.

1432
01:14:47,628 --> 01:14:49,162
Uh!

1433
01:14:54,100 --> 01:14:55,335
Ah!

1434
01:15:17,023 --> 01:15:18,124
Gucci, we are inbound.

1435
01:15:21,461 --> 01:15:22,462
Stay in the car.

1436
01:15:27,901 --> 01:15:29,069
- Moreno...
- On it!

1437
01:15:29,202 --> 01:15:30,303
SUV incoming!

1438
01:15:36,209 --> 01:15:37,644
Drone! Drone! Drone!

1439
01:15:37,778 --> 01:15:39,412
- Get the fuck outta there!
- Dunne!

1440
01:15:39,545 --> 01:15:41,481
Everyone down!

1441
01:15:47,387 --> 01:15:49,823
Dunne! Dunne!

1442
01:15:51,624 --> 01:15:52,458
Argh!

1443
01:16:02,135 --> 01:16:03,636
Argh!

1444
01:16:26,126 --> 01:16:27,527
Gucci, Moreno, get to the bikes!

1445
01:16:27,694 --> 01:16:29,095
On it. Let's go!

1446
01:16:30,496 --> 01:16:32,232
Change of plan! West evac.

1447
01:16:32,365 --> 01:16:34,200
We can't do that.
There's another team incoming.

1448
01:16:34,334 --> 01:16:36,269
Then we'll lose them
in the banana pie.

1449
01:16:38,038 --> 01:16:40,240
Baker, eyes out.
Keep us covered.

1450
01:16:48,381 --> 01:16:50,050
I've got eyes on.
They're one kilometer out.

1451
01:17:10,470 --> 01:17:12,905
Gucci, Moreno, peel off
and prepare to ram's horn.

1452
01:17:12,906 --> 01:17:14,339
Copy.

1453
01:17:23,716 --> 01:17:25,118
Baker, hold your fire.

1454
01:17:25,385 --> 01:17:26,419
Wait 'til they're deep
in the trap.

1455
01:17:30,690 --> 01:17:32,357
A hundred feet out.

1456
01:17:32,358 --> 01:17:33,359
Ram's horn, now!

1457
01:17:34,360 --> 01:17:35,128
Turning now.

1458
01:17:41,701 --> 01:17:43,369
Argh!

1459
01:17:52,512 --> 01:17:53,847
Baker, hold them back.

1460
01:17:57,884 --> 01:18:00,921
Bronco, stopping in three,
two, one...

1461
01:18:03,189 --> 01:18:03,890
Bronco's out.

1462
01:18:06,626 --> 01:18:07,493
Opening the pit.

1463
01:18:09,963 --> 01:18:11,097
Ah, fuck.

1464
01:18:11,397 --> 01:18:12,598
Pit don't open.

1465
01:18:12,799 --> 01:18:14,034
Bronco, I'm running
out of road here!

1466
01:18:14,200 --> 01:18:15,101
Make it fucking open!

1467
01:18:20,406 --> 01:18:22,075
Aaargh!

1468
01:18:23,209 --> 01:18:24,710
Aaargh!

1469
01:18:44,898 --> 01:18:45,832
Argh!

1470
01:18:51,237 --> 01:18:52,505
Bronco, are you good?

1471
01:18:52,638 --> 01:18:54,040
We're good.
See you at the villa.

1472
01:18:56,742 --> 01:18:59,846
Don't worry. There's 70 of us
and six of them.

1473
01:19:00,981 --> 01:19:02,048
Let's go!

1474
01:19:08,588 --> 01:19:09,822
Gucci, drone.

1475
01:19:09,956 --> 01:19:11,824
- Baker, jack-in-the-box.
- Copy.

1476
01:19:11,958 --> 01:19:14,127
Moreno, you'll be with me.
South side.

1477
01:19:14,260 --> 01:19:15,261
Aye aye, Sir.

1478
01:19:15,495 --> 01:19:16,696
We hold them off, draw them in,

1479
01:19:16,863 --> 01:19:18,264
rig this place
and blow the nest.

1480
01:19:20,833 --> 01:19:22,335
Drone is live.

1481
01:19:30,676 --> 01:19:32,412
Three vehicles on the west side.

1482
01:19:32,545 --> 01:19:33,379
Three hundred yards out.

1483
01:19:35,448 --> 01:19:36,549
Stinger, now.

1484
01:19:43,489 --> 01:19:44,724
Twelve on foot
coming your way, Sid.

1485
01:19:44,857 --> 01:19:45,892
They're heading over the ridge.

1486
01:19:49,229 --> 01:19:50,563
Two vehicles, east road.

1487
01:19:50,696 --> 01:19:51,697
Coming towards you, Bronco.

1488
01:19:52,865 --> 01:19:54,400
Baker.

1489
01:20:02,708 --> 01:20:04,044
First car is down!

1490
01:20:04,477 --> 01:20:05,378
Sid, they're cresting
the ridge.

1491
01:20:05,511 --> 01:20:06,512
- Moreno?
- Ready.

1492
01:20:06,679 --> 01:20:07,981
Engage.

1493
01:20:34,174 --> 01:20:35,408
Truck incoming,
east side!

1494
01:20:35,541 --> 01:20:37,377
Another SUV, south east.

1495
01:20:37,510 --> 01:20:39,312
Tactical with an M60
on their back.

1496
01:20:39,445 --> 01:20:40,213
I'll clear up.

1497
01:20:51,291 --> 01:20:53,193
- Baker, open the hole!
- Yes, Sir!

1498
01:21:05,305 --> 01:21:06,239
Moreno, on your right!

1499
01:21:09,875 --> 01:21:10,743
The hole's clear!

1500
01:21:19,152 --> 01:21:20,853
Gucci, Moreno, go ahead,

1501
01:21:20,987 --> 01:21:22,088
set up the zipline!

1502
01:21:22,255 --> 01:21:23,923
- Move!
- Moving.

1503
01:21:25,225 --> 01:21:26,426
Covering. Sid, move!

1504
01:21:30,430 --> 01:21:31,797
Gucci, let's go!

1505
01:21:32,498 --> 01:21:34,034
Check the route is clear.
Leave our ATV running.

1506
01:21:34,167 --> 01:21:35,035
Yes, Sir.

1507
01:21:35,168 --> 01:21:36,436
Move! Move it!

1508
01:21:36,669 --> 01:21:38,171
Move!

1509
01:21:48,781 --> 01:21:50,683
- How you doing, Baker?
- All good.

1510
01:21:51,151 --> 01:21:53,286
Charges are set. We're ready.

1511
01:21:54,087 --> 01:21:54,987
Evac's clear.

1512
01:22:04,264 --> 01:22:07,133
Bronco. Getting meat sweats.

1513
01:22:07,267 --> 01:22:08,401
Shall we ring the bell?

1514
01:22:10,036 --> 01:22:10,703
Thinking so.

1515
01:22:20,946 --> 01:22:22,014
Sid, zipline's up.

1516
01:22:23,049 --> 01:22:25,085
Bronco, Mum, let's go.

1517
01:22:25,685 --> 01:22:26,952
Get Mom out of here.
I'll catch you up.

1518
01:22:28,054 --> 01:22:29,455
No, it's too hot.

1519
01:22:29,622 --> 01:22:31,724
Don't fuck around. I'll stay.

1520
01:22:31,957 --> 01:22:33,559
The plan was you two with Mom.

1521
01:22:33,759 --> 01:22:35,095
Someone needs to stay
and press the fucking buttons.

1522
01:22:35,228 --> 01:22:36,896
- Baker!
- Don't fuck around!

1523
01:22:42,568 --> 01:22:43,336
Bronco...

1524
01:22:44,304 --> 01:22:45,205
Two minutes, Baker.

1525
01:22:45,471 --> 01:22:46,372
I'll be there.

1526
01:22:46,639 --> 01:22:47,407
Two minutes.

1527
01:22:48,741 --> 01:22:49,542
Time to go.

1528
01:22:56,249 --> 01:22:57,483
Rachel, stay close.

1529
01:23:08,694 --> 01:23:09,562
Sid!

1530
01:23:12,698 --> 01:23:13,433
Argh!

1531
01:23:14,434 --> 01:23:15,168
Stay covered.

1532
01:23:26,179 --> 01:23:28,148
Your ATV's running.
We're heading to the port.

1533
01:23:28,381 --> 01:23:29,649
¡Vamos! ¡Vamos!

1534
01:23:42,895 --> 01:23:44,330
Bronco, we need to move.

1535
01:23:44,464 --> 01:23:46,332
Baker,
what's your status?

1536
01:23:46,599 --> 01:23:48,668
- Baker?
- I'm on my way!

1537
01:23:49,535 --> 01:23:51,471
Baker, that's
two minutes. It's time to go.

1538
01:23:51,704 --> 01:23:52,938
I said I'm on my way.

1539
01:23:56,242 --> 01:23:57,943
Get out the front,
the tunnel's compromised.

1540
01:24:06,919 --> 01:24:07,653
Aargh!

1541
01:24:10,923 --> 01:24:12,325
Damn it, Baker! Come in!
What are you doing?

1542
01:24:12,458 --> 01:24:13,793
I'll meet you
at the extraction point.

1543
01:24:23,002 --> 01:24:24,704
- Baker!
- I'm right behind ya.

1544
01:24:24,837 --> 01:24:26,272
You're not fucking
behind me, Baker!

1545
01:24:26,439 --> 01:24:27,907
Get out of there!
That's an order!

1546
01:24:29,475 --> 01:24:30,443
That's an order!

1547
01:24:31,644 --> 01:24:32,412
Fuck!

1548
01:24:35,681 --> 01:24:37,650
Fuck. Just get Mom
off the island.

1549
01:24:37,783 --> 01:24:39,118
What are you doing?

1550
01:24:39,319 --> 01:24:41,521
Don't you do it!
Don't you fucking do it!

1551
01:24:41,654 --> 01:24:43,088
Baker! Baker!

1552
01:25:06,546 --> 01:25:07,647
Aargh!

1553
01:25:10,816 --> 01:25:11,884
Uh!

1554
01:25:31,637 --> 01:25:33,673
Rachel, with me!
Sid, let's go!

1555
01:25:46,486 --> 01:25:47,687
Moreno, Gucci,

1556
01:25:48,053 --> 01:25:49,422
we're two minutes
from the dock.

1557
01:25:49,555 --> 01:25:51,257
Copy. We're ready to go.

1558
01:26:10,510 --> 01:26:11,877
Ah!

1559
01:26:22,422 --> 01:26:23,889
Ah... urgh!

1560
01:26:24,023 --> 01:26:25,358
Shit!

1561
01:26:45,044 --> 01:26:46,278
Go around again!

1562
01:26:53,118 --> 01:26:53,886
Range?

1563
01:26:54,487 --> 01:26:55,287
Wait.

1564
01:26:58,157 --> 01:26:59,091
I said, "range."

1565
01:26:59,659 --> 01:27:00,893
I said, "wait."

1566
01:27:04,229 --> 01:27:07,600
Three hundred. Er, wait, 275.

1567
01:27:07,833 --> 01:27:09,569
- Make your mind up.
- 250. Ram it, Janet.

1568
01:27:13,473 --> 01:27:14,340
Aaah!

1569
01:27:49,975 --> 01:27:50,943
Come on.

1570
01:27:51,977 --> 01:27:52,712
Baker?

1571
01:27:54,213 --> 01:27:55,014
No.

1572
01:27:57,817 --> 01:27:58,718
Take her to the boat.

1573
01:28:00,653 --> 01:28:01,654
We'll catch you up.

1574
01:28:27,246 --> 01:28:29,181
I thought I'd stop by
on my way out.

1575
01:28:31,917 --> 01:28:33,152
No hard feelings, I hope?

1576
01:28:33,285 --> 01:28:35,020
Ah, I've been paid.

1577
01:28:35,488 --> 01:28:37,122
So, everyone's happy.

1578
01:28:37,356 --> 01:28:40,559
Well, not, not quite, actually.
I've come from upstairs.

1579
01:28:40,560 --> 01:28:41,927
So I see.

1580
01:28:42,662 --> 01:28:46,331
Seems like the whole Salazar
debacle continues to unfurl.

1581
01:28:48,100 --> 01:28:49,334
Why do I care?

1582
01:28:50,035 --> 01:28:52,638
No-one knows where he is.
He disappeared.

1583
01:28:52,938 --> 01:28:54,039
We'll catch you up.

1584
01:29:05,551 --> 01:29:06,552
Hey!

1585
01:29:26,238 --> 01:29:27,239
Mierda...

1586
01:29:49,294 --> 01:29:51,163
You crossed
the line, Bobby.

1587
01:29:51,430 --> 01:29:53,599
You should have taken your out
while you had the chance.

1588
01:29:53,733 --> 01:29:55,601
I solved this problem for you,

1589
01:29:55,735 --> 01:29:58,037
but you got greedy
and made a mess of it.

1590
01:29:58,303 --> 01:30:01,607
So, Sid and Bronco are now going
to solve it their way.

1591
01:30:01,774 --> 01:30:03,775
Someone needs to wear it.

1592
01:30:03,776 --> 01:30:05,310
Someone needs to be buried.

1593
01:30:07,079 --> 01:30:08,514
It's not gonna be me.

1594
01:30:09,148 --> 01:30:11,116
Well, let's just hope
Salazar doesn't turn up,

1595
01:30:11,250 --> 01:30:13,318
because if he does,
he'll turn state evidence

1596
01:30:13,452 --> 01:30:14,787
on Spencer Goldstein

1597
01:30:15,020 --> 01:30:16,756
for funding
a criminal organisation.

1598
01:30:16,922 --> 01:30:18,924
Welcome to Miami, Mr. Salazar.

1599
01:30:24,496 --> 01:30:25,931
Who the fuck is Mr. Salazar?

1600
01:30:27,032 --> 01:30:28,100
I'm Mr. Smith.

1601
01:30:30,002 --> 01:30:32,104
As long as that little
red phone doesn't ring,

1602
01:30:33,205 --> 01:30:34,373
I'm sure you'll be fine.

1603
01:30:36,375 --> 01:30:37,309
Love you, Bobby.

